{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsYALAuEfU2Zb27WhwxN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NHWMonjYMJ4EJQN1JrKpuv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t14/primary/exec-ws/first-derivation.md","content":"# First derivation (method A: exact scaled-integer arithmetic)\n\nAuthored at node `propose-child` by X-E6. This file is the first derivation's\nintermediate work. It is intentionally EXCLUDED from the child's input\nmanifest so the E-B non-consultation condition holds.\n\n## Method A statement\n\nEach input is treated as an exact decimal string; binary floating point is\nnever used. For each input:\n\n1. Parse the string into sign, integer-part digit string `I`, and\n   fraction-part digit string `F` (empty if no `.`).\n2. Scale the unsigned value by 10^2 exactly: the integer quotient\n   `Q = int(I ++ first-two-digits-of-F-padded-with-zeros)` and the exact\n   remainder `r = 0.<remaining fraction digits>` (an exact decimal in\n   [0, 1), i.e. the value of the fraction digits beyond position 2).\n3. Round: increment `Q` by 1 iff `r > 1/2`, or `r = 1/2` exactly and `Q`\n   is odd (ties to the even neighbor). Otherwise keep `Q`.\n4. Render `Q` as `<integer part>.<two decimals>` (Q div 100, Q mod 100\n   zero-padded), group the integer part with commas every three digits.\n5. If the original sign was negative and the value is nonzero, wrap the\n   unsigned rendering in parentheses.\n\n## Per-item work\n\n| input       | Q (scaled)  | r    | Q parity | rounded Q  | formatted        |\n|-------------|-------------|------|----------|------------|------------------|\n| 2.675       | 267         | 1/2  | odd      | 268        | 2.68             |\n| -1234.5     | 123450      | 0    | —        | 123450     | (1,234.50)       |\n| 0.005       | 0           | 1/2  | even     | 0          | 0.00             |\n| 1000        | 100000      | 0    | —        | 100000     | 1,000.00         |\n| -0.125      | 12          | 1/2  | even     | 12         | (0.12)           |\n| 999999.995  | 99999999    | 1/2  | odd      | 100000000  | 1,000,000.00     |\n| 0.045       | 4           | 1/2  | even     | 4          | 0.04             |\n| 12345.675   | 1234567     | 1/2  | odd      | 1234568    | 12,345.68        |\n| -2.5        | 250         | 0    | —        | 250        | (2.50)           |\n| 0           | 0           | 0    | —        | 0          | 0.00             |\n| 7.375       | 737         | 1/2  | odd      | 738        | 7.38             |\n| -999.985    | 99998       | 1/2  | even     | 99998      | (999.98)         |\n\nNotes on the adversarial traps, handled exactly:\n\n- Every `...5`-terminated item has remainder exactly 1/2 under exact\n  decimal treatment (never 0.49999... as under binary float parsing).\n- Carry propagation: 999999.995 rounds up across all digits to\n  1,000,000.00.\n- Sign ordering is irrelevant under half-even (symmetric about zero); the\n  unsigned value is rounded and the sign applied as parentheses.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":494,"cache_read_input_tokens":42272,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":494},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bac46f26-2add-49b9-a447-36715bced814","uuid":"716821f6-8000-4dd2-b317-51d8dcbf2195","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:06:37.043Z","request_id":"req_011CdsYAHSCaQFYgZGqMobUN"}
